<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Johnnic raises yr shr, offers scrip award.</title>
<headline>Johnnic raises yr shr, offers scrip award.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Equity accounted shr (cts)  326.0 vs 233.0</p>
<p>    Headline shr (cts)	    287.0 vs 202.0</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)		  72.0 vs  50.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income		   123.6 vs 236.5</p>
<p>    Equity accounted earnings   489.5 vs 346.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   126.0 vs 243.2</p>
<p>    Tax				   2.3 vs   6.5</p>
<p>    Turnover			  279.2 vs 200.5</p>
<p>Div payable Oct 25</p>
<p>on register Sept 13</p>
<p>Full name: Johnnic Industrial Corp Ltd</p>
<p>    Share of associates'  365.9   vs 109.9</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it had resolved to offer capitalisation shares to shareholders on register on Sept 13.</p>
<p>It said shareholders could elect to receive a cash dividend instead. The number of new shares to be issued would be in the ratio that 76 cents bears to the weighted average traded price of Johnnic shares on the JSE for the three days ending October 17. The new shares to be issued pursuant to the capitalisation award will be issued as fully paid shares of 10 cents each.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
